{
  "name": "ant",
  "_about": "A red wood ant worker (Formica rufa), 8 mm long: three parts on a waist -- a big head with toothed jaws and elbowed antennae (a long scape, then a whip of eleven joints), a narrow humped mesosoma carrying the six long legs, a one-noded petiole, and the round gaster; reddish on the face and the mesosoma, the crown and the gaster black-brown. Coats: the black garden ant (Lasius niger, 4 mm, all dark) and the yellow meadow ant. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/bugs.py on insectlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
